  "reconstruction": {
    "candidateId": "N0517",
    "scope": "Temple of Peace present-day visible ruins: seven mapped re-erected plain pink granite shafts on white stepped bases/stylobate, roofless low brick/concrete court traces, fallen drums and fragments, patchy paving in the exposed western court, and eight low mapped eastern relics. The intervening native terrain is preserved. Keep the independent Santi Cosma e Damiano church, later structures, Basilica of Maxentius, Nerva and neighboring Roman Forum. No intact Roman roof, entablature or lost superstructure is reconstructed.",
    "identityBasis": "Q1456939/relation1841167 identifies three separated archaeological areas, not a solid building. Seven individual pinned PMTiles column footprints determine the standing row. Its own measured map axis controls the internal architecture, rather than applying the broad precinct bounding-box axis to every shaft. Eight small eastern mapped remnants are low fragment treatments. Native+X east/+Z south and runtime heading0. Only the visible western court has an authored ground surface. Other archaeological boundary polygons do not imply invented building masses or paved platforms. Later neighboring footprints stay independent.",
    "heightBasis": "Two ordinary current-state photographs guide approximate shafts6.8m tall above the white bases, a1.35m stepped stylobate and low0.35–2.2m broken walls. No capitals/entablature are invented. Fallen drums, paving patches, low court rectangles, small fragment height and erosion are picture-led visualization estimates, not surveyed inventories.",
    "terrainBasis": "Reused pinned N0506 standard Rome PMTiles/Mapzen extract. Only the photographed western court receives a shallow visualization pavement above its local coarse grid, with buried retaining foundations and stepped colonnade. Unverified intervening/southeastern precinct surfaces stay native; eight eastern mapped remnants sit locally on the original terrain. No ground or water opening. Exact excavated depths and street retaining levels remain approximate.",
    "architecturalAngleRadians": 0.8636675509419043,
